        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Why programs are built from functions:</strong></span>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A change happens in one place.</strong> Add a trading fee inside <code>compute_cost</code> and every portfolio's cost follows.</li>\n<li><strong>The name says what the work is for.</strong> <code>compute_cost(retirement_holdings)</code> reads as a sentence; a loop has to be read line by line.</li>\n<li><strong>Everything it needs comes in through the brackets.</strong> So you can test it on a portfolio whose answer you already know, such as notebook 3's $116,302.70.</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ROlb",
      "code_hash": "30bc962c16a83e62af1603e2656f8ec1",
