    {
      "id": "oyMU",
      "code_hash": "cdee767716722c7f175246dc0f1a251b",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><code>result</code> holds <code>None</code>. <code>count_shares_print</code> has no <code>return</code>, so calling it gives back nothing, even though it printed <code>600</code> on its way out. <code>print</code> only displays a value; it does not hand it back to the line that called the function. The next cell cannot do anything with <code>result</code>, since there is no number in it to add, compare, or pass to another function\u2014only the empty value <code>None</code>.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nHfw",
      "code_hash": "ddcc597ad8d2a511c60b96b824e2527a",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"2-calling-an-api\">2. Calling an API</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Calling an <strong>API</strong> is like calling a function someone else wrote, running on their computer. You call it with a web address, their server runs its code, and the result comes back to you.</span>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Calling a function you wrote</th>\n<th>Calling an API</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>You call it with</strong></td>\n<td><code>get_towns(\"Norfolk\")</code></td>\n<td><code>oim.zhili.dev/ma/towns?county=Norfolk</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>What goes in</strong></td>\n<td>parameters in brackets</td>\n<td>parameters after <code>?</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>What comes back</strong></td>\n<td>the <code>return</code> value</td>\n<td>a reply, usually JSON</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>When it goes wrong</strong></td>\n<td>an error in your notebook</td>\n<td>a status code and a message</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Where it runs</strong></td>\n<td>your laptop</td>\n<td>somebody else's server</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">You cannot see the code behind an API, so its documentation is how you learn its parameters and what it returns.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "xXTn",
      "code_hash": "554e289048502368930abe609e37acf7",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The course runs its own API at <code>oim.zhili.dev</code>. Its Massachusetts endpoints come from the state's <a href=\"https://www.mass.gov/info-details/division-of-local-services-municipal-databank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">Division of Local Services</a>: every city and town, its population and income, and its property tax rates and bills. The documentation is at <a href=\"https://oim.zhili.dev/docs\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">oim.zhili.dev/docs</a>, and the API also lists its own endpoints. <strong>Before any code</strong>, open <a href=\"https://oim.zhili.dev/mass\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">oim.zhili.dev/mass</a> and <a href=\"https://oim.zhili.dev/ma/towns?county=Norfolk\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">oim.zhili.dev/ma/towns?county=Norfolk</a> in your browser and read what comes back. <code>requests</code> is already in your project from notebook 3.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
