            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"d-from-a-name-to-a-history\">\u270f\ufe0f D \u00b7 From a Name to a History</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>Find Wellesley's <code>dor_code</code> with the <code>name</code> parameter of <code>/ma/towns</code>.</li>\n<li>Use it to ask <code>/ma/towns/{dor_code}/history</code> for fiscal year 2026.</li>\n<li>Check the bill a second way: the average value times the tax rate, divided by 1,000.</li>\n</ol>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><em>Check yourself: <code>317</code>. Then $2,020,758 \u00d7 10.17 / 1,000 = $20,551.11, and the reply's bill is $20,551.</em></span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>Going further.</strong> Write <code>town_history(name)</code>, which takes a town's name, makes both requests, and returns the history.</span></span>"
